' 18 Scan driver: RECEIVE-SCAN of a bag or a set, with RESTORE-SCAN.
'
' Source of Figure N11.2 in ../design.md (section N11.2). The figure restates
' the receive plan of rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/disciplines/scan.rs
' and the fire count of the transaction (Cx::rounds in spaces/generic.rs,
' plan revision I-21). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The plan opens: the settle before it runs, and a full transaction
'      re-issues the receive before it stages anything (open_plan).
'   2. The driver visits the records in the pick order of the receive and
'      takes the first record whose payload the pattern binds.
'   3. The guard is checked once, on that record. A refusal parks the
'      receive (decision 37).
'   4. The fire counts first. A peek of a non-persistent record then sends
'      the record again (RESTORE-SCAN, decision 45 Rule E).
'   5. A second send that meets a full transaction re-issues before it fires.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 18-scan-driver.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 18-scan-driver
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
title RECEIVE-SCAN with RESTORE-SCAN (the bag, P5a)

start
:open_plan: the settle before the plan; <<$rrs_agent>>
if (the transaction made FIRE_ROUND_CAP fires?) then (yes)
  :re-issue the receive (RoundCap)
  stage nothing; <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
while (a record is left in the pick order of the receive?) is (yes)
  if (the pattern binds the payload?) then (yes)
    break
  else (no)
    :next record (one decode); <<$rrs_storage>>
  endif
endwhile (no)
if (a record r was found and the guard admits it?) then (yes)
  :count the fire on the transaction
  (FireRounds::after_fire); <<$rrs_agent>>
  :stage Fire(K, [r]); <<$rrs_effect>>
  if (K peeks and r is not persistent?) then (yes)
    if (the transaction is full?) then (yes)
      :re-issue the second send of r
      (a produce of its payload); <<$rrs_reject>>
    else (no)
      :RESTORE-SCAN: OFFER-SCAN of r
      with the identity and the authority of r; <<$rrs_flow>>
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
else (no)
  :park K (the guard is checked once); <<$rrs_storage>>
endif
stop
@enduml
